"""
@@@ replace
miss.  ``disable`` invalidates the cache entry immediately; other instances learn about it after
the positive-cache TTL (documented revocation lag).

Links with a click limit (``max_clicks``) never take their allowance from the cache: the cached
entry only says "limited" (the limit is immutable), and every redirect consumes one click with a
single atomic conditional UPDATE (``LinkRepository.consume_click``).  A refusal means the
allowance is used up: the entry is dropped and the request answers 410.  The background click
writer leaves the counter of limited links alone, so a click is never counted twice.
"""
@@@ end

